Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The subgraph with the given vertices and edges, as a lazy view (JGraphT’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsSubgraph"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Mathematica’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Subgraph"},{"type":"text","text":"): an edge is kept when it is listed and both its ends are kept, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a listed edge with an end outside "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" is dropped. Vertices are numbered as for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inducedSubgraph(on:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and edge indices as for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"spanningSubgraph(edges:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/subgraph(vertices:edges:)","kind":"symbol","title":"subgraph(vertices:edges:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/subgraph(vertices:edges:)","role":"symbol"}}}